<title>USA: Air-Cure sells two subsidiaries.</title>
<headline>Air-Cure sells two subsidiaries.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air-Cure Technologies Inc said on Wednesday it sold two of its subsidiaries for $1.7 million, a sum somewhat equal to the company's investment in those operations.</p>
<p>The subsidiaries, Air-Cure Inc and Pipkorn Environmental Technologies Inc, are involved in the manufacture of baghouse systems and generated sales revenue of approximately $5 million from combined operations as well as an incurred loss in the company's past fiscal year.</p>
<p>The company did not identify the buyer in a statement obtained by Reuters.</p>
<p>Air-Cure Technologies is a supplier of manufactured equipment and engineered systems.</p>
